      "questionText": "Consider a water tank shown in the figure. It has one wall at x = L and can be taken to be very wide in the z direction. When filled with a liquid of surface tension S and density ρ, the liquid surface makes angle θ0 (θ0 << 1) with the x-axis at x = L. If y(x) is the height of the surface then the equation for y(x) is:",
